> as:
>  cupra     pra      produce                                   x1 produces
> x2 [product] by process
> x3                                                           8f  22    (cf.
> zbasu, farvi, gundi, jukpa)
>
> Now, how does this differ from {finti} and {zbasu}?
>
> Cars are assembled repetitively from sub-assemblies and componets (zbasu).
> Gasoline/petrol is produced by a continuous process (cupra).
> Paintings (usually) are created once only and are unique (finti).
>
> There are of course an infinite number of 'in-between' situations.  The
> challenge
> then in lojban is the same as in anyother language.  Either special terms
> like
> 'batch processing' are invented, or whole sentences are needed to
> facilitate
> understanding.
